A hook whose first token is neither `script` nor `set` exits 2 naming the verb. The
status set runs as the edge's first hook, so the artifact already carries the target status when the
unknown verb aborts the run.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: never — the hook verb is unknown
            hooks: ["teleport somewhere"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
booping transition run/index.md intaking --playbook fx-hooks
booping transition run/index.md noted --playbook fx-hooks
-- exit --
2
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
-- stderr --
error: unknown hook: 'teleport'
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: noted
---
